  "chitchat": [
    "throws a stone at the Curtain. Nothing happens.",
    "\"One day it'll bounce.\"",
    "\"I'm not wasting stones. I'm counting.\""
  ],
  "description": "A wiry teenager in a hoodie three sizes up, pockets heavy with stones from the lane. His knuckles are grazed. Every so often he throws one at the Curtain, which takes it without a sound.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "What have you got against the Architect?",
          "next": "gripe"
        },
        {
          "label": "Bye.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Jubal keeps throwing. \"What?\"",
      "text_by_relation": {
        "first": "The kid in the oversized hoodie doesn't stop throwing. A stone goes into the Curtain without a sound.\n\n\"Jubal. Don't tell me it's pointless, Gresley tells me every day.\" He picks up another stone. \"Everyone here grew up being told it keeps us safe. Safe in here. Never asked if we wanted in.\"",
        "known": "\"You again.\" He offers you a stone. \"Go on.\"",
        "familiar": "Jubal hands you a good flat stone, his second best.\n\n\"Aim low. I've done high.\""
      }
    },
    "gripe": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Right.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"My mum came through the South Gate with me in a sling and they let us in and never let us out.\" He throws. \"Nobody hits you. Nobody locks a door. There's just a wall where the rest of the world was. That's worse. You can't even be angry at a person.\""
    },
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "Jubal goes back to the lane."
    }
  },
